  "limitations": [
    "Five alternating pairs; warmups excluded. Paired ratios use cohort index, not pooled medians. No significance claim.",
    "Direct control consumes Arrow batches; PG executor is EXPLAIN ANALYZE TIMING OFF; COPY includes full binary delivery. These are different scopes.",
    "Profile CPU includes profiling overhead and twenty scans. Do not compare it to unprofiled wall time as if clocks were interchangeable.",
    "Sample categories are inclusive and overlap. Inlining, unresolved frames, and truncated stacks can hide matcher work.",
    "Any-unresolved counts include system-library and PostgreSQL frames, not just extension frames. A stack counts once even with several unresolved frames; unresolved work cannot be assigned confidently.",
    "Both profiles use perf --no-inline with exact saved ELF symbols and DWARF unwinding; no synthetic inline expansion. Resolved symbols alone cannot recover inlined Matcher::is_match boundaries.",
    "Single CPU profile per workload/binary cannot establish a robust halving of true non-matcher overhead.",
    "Shared-host background activity is not controlled by this report; host-load ranges describe recorded conditions, not causal attribution.",
    "Exact-value controls are persisted runner attestations; raw COPY/Arrow payloads are not retained for independent value replay.",
    "SHA consistency does not itself prove build reproducibility; source commits and flags are recorded in build-provenance.json."
  ],
  "non_matcher_definition": "Non-matcher sampled share = weight of stacks with neither a visible Matcher::is_match frame nor a regex, regex_automata, or aho_corasick frame / total folded stack weight. The intended boundary excludes the whole Matcher::is_match call, including its view/scratch work; engine frames also identify matcher samples when that caller is inlined or missing. The JSON reports complements of visible Matcher::is_match alone and engine frames alone separately, plus their union used for the proxy. This complement includes PostgreSQL, FDW, transport, conversion, wrapper, view/cache work, unresolved frames, and matcher work hidden by inlining or incomplete unwinding. It is not an exclusive stage measurement. Both binaries use perf --no-inline and exact saved ELF symbols: recorded DWARF-unwound frames have no synthetic inline-frame expansion. Therefore even fully resolved ELF symbols do not reveal all inlined Matcher::is_match work; the complements cannot exactly isolate everything outside that call. Estimated non-matcher user CPU/row = process user CPU/row times that share. cycles:u sampling and process CPU ticks measure different quantities; this multiplication is an attribution proxy, not exact CPU accounting. System CPU is reported separately and is not apportioned by user-only samples.",
  "profile_symbolization": {
    "perf_version": "perf version 6.12.117",
    "symbolization": "perf --no-inline with exact saved ELF: real DWARF-unwound frames; no synthetic inline expansion"
  },
